# Jira register (live-read 2026-08-21)

- Cloud: `https://eliteintegrityservices.atlassian.net` — project **P2024** (Elite Integrity - Engineering)
- REST v3 with operator email + API token. **Never store tokens in this folder.**
- Types: **Project** (job) → **Task** (package) → **Sub-task** (drawing). Dummy job `P2024-15553` spawned this template.

## Pack list = every issue with this Job Number

- Search: `project = P2024 AND issuetype != Project AND "Job Number" ~ "{job}"` (Tasks, Sub-tasks, EDDI items — not only `labels = Drafting`).
- Also walk the job **Project** issue for that Job Number: direct children and their sub-tasks, even when Job Number was never copied onto those issues.
- After Load, show that **Project** issue’s summary and key (dummy `P2024-15553`) next to the matched or Located Dropbox job folder. Several Job Numbers may share one folder; they stay two Loads / two register lists.
- Group on the console by EDDI Status (1–9), header row between groups. Blank EDDI → Ungrouped. **0 Generic is not listed.**
- Missing PDF: **Locate…** on the row (pairs the file; does not rewrite Jira). **Locate…** stays after a match so the operator can pick a different file. **Open** beside it opens the paired PDF in the Windows default reader (disabled until a file is paired; missing file is a short error). The file picker remembers the last folder on this PC (LOCALAPPDATA, not Dropbox).
- Drawings are still Sub-tasks under the Drawing Package (label `Drafting`). Dummy drawings: `P2024-15578` `2026-Tanzim-1-1 Drawing-1`, `P2024-15579` `2026-Tanzim-1-2 Drawing-2`
- Live summary shape: ID is the leading code (`2026-075-1-STWD`, `2026-075-ITP-1-1`); wording after that is the description. Empty description is fine. Job Number field is the grouping key.

## Field map

| Use | Field | ID |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Job | Job Number | `customfield_10300` |
| Due date | Due date | `duedate` (not edited on the console; Confirm writes it from Return Request Date when that Next date is entered) |
| Client Doc No. | Client Document Number | `customfield_10279` (text) |
| Outgoing revision | Outgoing Rev | `customfield_10280` |
| Submitted to Client For | Submitted to Client For | `customfield_10281` (Approval / Info / Planned / NA) |
| Submission Date | Submission Date | `customfield_10301` |
| Return Request Date | Return Request Date | `customfield_10046` |
| Incoming rev | Incoming Rev | `customfield_10283` |
| Client Approval Status | Client Approval Status | `customfield_10284` (Approved / Approved with Comments / Revise & Resubmit / Rejected / Info / Void) |
| Return Date | Return Date | `customfield_10066` |
| Shop IFC Rev / Date | Shop IFC Rev / Shop IFC Date | `customfield_10285` / `customfield_10286` |
| Field IFC Rev / Date | Field IFC Rev / Field IFC Date | `customfield_10287` / `customfield_10288` |
| EDDI Status | EDDI Status | `customfield_10289` (multi-checkbox; DocCon needs one option). On Load, more than one value prompts for a single 1–9 choice, writes that, and reloads. Skip continues Load with the messy multi-status. Generic (0) is not listed on the board. |

All of those (plus workflow **Status**) except **Due Date** are Now/Next on the pack board. Confirm writes filled Next values, and writes Jira Due Date from a newly entered Return Request Date. Cover Date issued / Expected return stay on the Excel letter (not Jira fields by themselves). Load starts both at N/A with Pack off. Expected return stamps packed Next Return Request Date (`customfield_10046`) to the same calendar day; Confirm writes that to Jira and copies a newly entered value to `duedate`. Cover Date issued stamps packed Next Submission Date (`customfield_10301`) the same way. Setting a cover date back to N/A restores that packed Next date to Now. Pack-tick with blank/N/A does not wipe a typed Next. Blank Expected return → N/A on the letter. Blank/N/A Date issued → today on the letter. Submitted to Client For, Client Approval Status, Shop/Field IFC Rev, and EDDI Status are pick-only lists (same as Status).

Sub-task statuses: To Do, In Progress, OFA, Awaiting Client Information, Roadblock, Back from Client, IFI, IFC, Done.

Template also has Task `Document Transmittals` (label `DocCon`) — a work package, not the drawing register.

Log numbering (locked 2026-09-01): `CT|ST|FT-{Job Number}-{n}` from the job Excel books under `3.0 Doc Con`. Client STATUS list: APPROVAL, CONSTRUCTION, INFORMATION, REVIEW, AS-BUILT (not the same labels as Jira purpose).

Controllers today edit those fields in a Jira Excel export. That file is not a second register. They will edit the same fields **on the DocCon console**; confirm writes Jira REST on the drawing sub-task.

